{"explanation":"Sum all values with a plain loop (no mutation of the input) and divide by the length. With at most 100 finite values of magnitude <=1000, the sum is finite and the result is a finite Number. Negative zero is normalized to 0 to keep the JSON-serializable value clean.","code":"function solve(values) {
