{"explanation":"Classic 0/1 knapsack solved with a 1D dynamic programming array iterated from high capacity down to the item weight, so each item is used at most once. dp[c] holds the best value achievable with total weight <= c. Inputs are only read, never mutated. The result is a plain Number (max value is at most 1200), so it is finite and JSON-safe. Edge cases: empty arrays or capacity 0 return 0.","code":"function solve(weights, values, capacity) {
  var n = Math.min(weights.length, values.length);
  var cap = capacity | 0;
  if (cap < 0) cap = 0;
  var dp = new Array(cap + 1);
  for (var c = 0; c <= cap; c++) dp[c] = 0;
  for (var i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    var w = weights[i];
    var v = values[i];
    for (var j = cap; j >= w; j--) {
      var cand = dp[j - w] + v;
      if (cand > dp[j]) dp[j] = cand;
    }
  }
  return Number(dp[cap]);
}"}

{"explanation":"Classic wildcard matching via dynamic programming. dp[i][j] is true if the first i chars of text match the first j chars of pattern. dp[0][0]=true; a '*' at pattern position j lets dp[0][j] inherit dp[0][j-1]. For each cell: '*' matches if dp[i][j-1] (empty) or dp[i-1][j] (consume one more text char); '?' matches if dp[i-1][j-1]; a literal matches if the characters are equal and dp[i-1][j-1]. Inputs are only read, never mutated, and the result is a plain boolean.","code":"function solve(text, pattern) {
  var n = text.length;
  var m = pattern.length;
  var dp = [];
  for (var i = 0; i <= n; i++) {
    var row = [];
    for (var j = 0; j <= m; j++) row.push(false);
    dp.push(row);
  }
  dp[0][0] = true;
  for (var j = 1; j <= m; j++) {
    if (pattern.charAt(j - 1) === '*') dp[0][j] = dp[0][j - 1];
  }
  for (var i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (var j = 1; j <= m; j++) {
      var p = pattern.charAt(j - 1);
      if (p === '*') {
        dp[i][j] = dp[i][j - 1] || dp[i - 1][j];
      } else if (p === '?') {
        dp[i][j] = dp[i - 1][j - 1];
      } else {
        dp[i][j] = dp[i - 1][j - 1] && text.charAt(i - 1) === p;
      }
    }
  }
  return dp[n][m] === true;
}"}

{"code":"function solve(weights, values, capacity) {
  const dp = new Array(capacity + 1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 0; i < weights.length; i++) {
    const w = weights[i], v = values[i];
    for (let c = capacity; c >= w; c--) {
      const t = dp[c - w] + v;
      if (t > dp[c]) dp[c] = t;
    }
  }
  return dp[capacity];
}"}

{"explanation":"This is the digital root. For n = 0 the result is 0. For n > 0 the digital root is 1 + (n - 1) % 9, which equals repeatedly summing digits until one digit remains. It uses only Number arithmetic, which is exact for n up to 1e9, and it does not mutate anything.","code":"function solve(n) {
  if (n === 0) return 0;
  return 1 + ((n - 1) % 9);
}"}

{"code":"function solve(a,b){
  if(a===b)return true;
  if(a===null||b===null||typeof a!=='object'||typeof b!=='object')return typeof a==='number'&&typeof b==='number'?(a===b||(a!==a&&b!==b)):false;
  const aa=Array.isArray(a),ba=Array.isArray(b);
  if(aa!==ba)return false;
  if(aa){
    if(a.length!==b.length)return false;
    for(let i=0;i<a.length;i++)if(!solve(a[i],b[i]))return false;
    return true;
  }
  const ka=Object.keys(a),kb=Object.keys(b);
  if(ka.length!==kb.length)return false;
  const has=Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty;
  for(const k of ka){
    if(!has.call(b,k)||!solve(a[k],b[k]))return false;
  }
  return true;
}"}

