{"explanation":"Return '' for an empty array. Otherwise take the first string as the candidate prefix and shorten it while comparing against each other string, character by character, stopping early once the prefix is empty. Inputs are only read, never mutated, and the result is always a string.","code":"function solve(strings) {
  if (!Array.isArray(strings) || strings.length === 0) return '';
  var prefix = String(strings[0]);
  for (var i = 1; i < strings.length && prefix.length > 0; i++) {
    var s = String(strings[i]);
    var n = Math.min(prefix.length, s.length);
    var j = 0;
    while (j < n && prefix.charCodeAt(j) === s.charCodeAt(j)) j++;
    prefix = prefix.slice(0, j);
  }
  return prefix;
}"}

