{"explanation":"Evaluate the RPN expression with a stack. Push each numeric token (parsed with Number), and for each operator (+, -, *) pop the right operand then the left operand, apply the operation, and push the result. The tokens array is only read, never mutated. The final stack value is returned. A result of -0 (e.g. 0 * -5) is normalized to 0 by adding 0 so the output stays JSON-safe and consistent.","code":"function solve(tokens) {
  const stack = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < tokens.length; i++) {
    const t = tokens[i];
    if (t === '+' || t === '-' || t === '*') {
      const b = stack.pop();
      const a = stack.pop();
      if (t === '+') stack.push(a + b);
      else if (t === '-') stack.push(a - b);
      else stack.push(a * b);
    } else {
      stack.push(Number(t));
    }
  }
  const result = stack.pop();
  return result === 0 ? 0 : result;
}"}

{"explanation":"Convert each of the three channel integers to a base-16 string with toString(16), left-pad with a zero to two characters, concatenate them with a leading '#'. toString(16) already yields lowercase digits. The input array is only read, never mutated.","code":"function solve(rgb) {
