{"explanation":"Walk the matrix with four boundaries (top, bottom, left, right). Traverse the top row left to right, then the right column top to bottom, then the bottom row right to left (if rows remain), then the left column bottom to top (if columns remain), shrinking the boundaries after each pass. Inputs are only read, never mutated, and the result is a new flat array.","code":"function solve(matrix) {
  var result = [];
  var top = 0;
  var bottom = matrix.length - 1;
  var left = 0;
  var right = matrix[0].length - 1;
  var i;
  while (top <= bottom && left <= right) {
    for (i = left; i <= right; i++) result.push(matrix[top][i]);
    top++;
    for (i = top; i <= bottom; i++) result.push(matrix[i][right]);
    right--;
    if (top <= bottom) {
      for (i = right; i >= left; i--) result.push(matrix[bottom][i]);
      bottom--;
    }
    if (left <= right) {
      for (i = bottom; i >= top; i--) result.push(matrix[i][left]);
      left++;
    }
  }
  return result;
}"}

{"code":"function solve(strings) {
