}"}

{"explanation": "Spreadsheet column labels use bijective base-26. Repeatedly subtract 1 from n, take n % 26 as the index of the next letter (0=A..25=Z), prepend it, then set n = floor(n / 26). Loop until n is 0. For example, 26 gives 'Z' and 27 gives 'AA'. Only core ECMAScript is used and nothing is mutated.", "code": "function solve(n) {
