}"}

{"explanation":"Use the patience-sorting approach: maintain an array 'tails' where tails[i] is the smallest possible tail of a strictly increasing subsequence of length i+1. For each value, binary search for the first tail >= value (lower bound) and replace it, or append if none exists. Strictness is handled by lower bound (equal values replace rather than extend). The answer is tails.length. Input is not mutated; empty input returns 0. Runs in O(n log n).","code":"function solve(values) {
